# Build-context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# This file is read by ``docker build`` when the context is
# ``backend/`` (see homelabsetup/deploy-homelab.sh:346). Without it,
# Docker tries to ship every file under backend/ to the daemon — which
# (a) makes the context huge (~70 MB before this file), (b) breaks on
# Windows when pytest-owned directories like ``.pytest_cache`` are
# permission-locked, and (c) busts the image cache on unrelated edits
# (a single test run changes ``.pytest_cache/v/cache/lastfailed`` and
# invalidates every cached layer after COPY).

# ── Python build artifacts / caches ──────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
# pytest --basetemp directories. The repo's own test instructions tell
# you to pass `--basetemp=backend/.pytest_tmp` on Windows, and sessions
# routinely use suffixed variants (.pytest_tmp_ui003_full, ...). Those
# directories are permission-locked on Windows, so podman/docker aborts
# the whole build reading their extended attributes:
#   copier: get: getting extended attributes for "/.pytest_tmp_...":
#   permission denied
# The bare `.pytest_cache` entries above did not cover them, so the
# documented test command broke the documented build.
.pytest_tmp*/
**/.pytest_tmp*/
# Custom pytest --basetemp roots used by local/CI validation (for example,
# `.tmp/pytest-homelab-full-*`) have the same Windows permission behavior.
.tmp/
**/.tmp/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ── Local virtualenvs (don't ship into the image) ────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Secrets / per-developer config ───────────────────────────────────
# .env files contain DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET_KEY, LLM API keys, etc.
# Production config is injected via k8s Secrets — never via image bake.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ── IDE / OS clutter ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ── Test artifacts the SDK build context staging leaves behind ───────
# (deploy-homelab.sh stages client SDKs INTO backend/clients/ before
# building; pytest_cache from a prior local run can be there too.)
clients/**/__pycache__/
clients/**/.pytest_cache/
clients/**/target/
clients/**/node_modules/

# ── Documentation / READMEs that don't need to be in the image ───────
README.md
*.md
docs/
